course: dictionary
lesson: 1065
title: Bough: an old word for a branch
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bough is a large, main branch of a tree. Everyday people usually say «branch», but a bough is the big arm that grows out of the trunk. You will meet it in stories, poems and songs.
explain: Look at the Cheshire Cat in Alice: it is «sitting on a bough (a branch) of a tree». The brackets tell you the meaning. Writers often put a simpler word beside a hard one, so look for brackets, dashes or commas that give you a clue.
explain: Bough also appears in the rhyme «Rock-a-bye Baby», where «the bough breaks». Here the word stays the same, but the sound is the tricky part, so say it slowly and think about the rhyme.
fact: A bough is a large, main branch of a tree.
fact: «Bough» is slightly old-fashioned or poetic; in everyday talk people say «branch».
fact: «Boughs» is the plural, which means more than one bough.
fact: Bough sounds like «cow», which makes it one of the -ough words that all sound different: though, through, tough, cough and thought.
fact: Phrases like «the bough breaks» and «boughs of holly» are often found in rhymes and songs.
exercise: «The cat sat on a bough of the apple tree.» What is a bough? | A type of fruit | *A large, main branch of a tree | A small leaf | A sharp gust of wind
exercise: «The boughs of holly were hung above the door.» Which everyday word could replace boughs here? | flowers | roots | leaves | *branches
exercise: Which word sounds like bough? | boat | bottle | bow | *cow
test: «The bird sang from the bough of the oak.» What does bough mean? | *a big branch | a root | the trunk | a leaf
test: Which everyday word is used instead of bough in most talk? | *branch | seed | root | trunk
exam: «The Cheshire Cat is sitting on a bough (a branch) of a tree.» What do the brackets tell us bough means? | *a branch | a bird's nest | a long claw | a tooth
